One final provenance wording correction: README, vector description and checker text call the two entries_root values “real Merkle over H(JCS(entry))”, but the vector supplies no {submission_seq, binding_cc, subject} entry pre-images and the checker deliberately does not verify membership. Therefore “real Merkle root” is currently asserted, not recomputable.
The clean fix consistent with option (b) is to call these well-formed opaque entries_root fixture values and explicitly make no derivation/membership claim. A dedicated membership suite can prove real roots later.
Also update the PR body: it still says 6 cases and lacks the new abstract-chain scope; current state is 7 cases.
With those wording corrections, the chain-completeness implementation itself is clean to merge. No dedicated membership suite is required for this PR.

